In article <482@norvax.UUCP> nell@norvax.UUCP (Russell Nell) writes:

>	I think I found a bug in 3.0.  I was sacrificing a corpse at an
>    alter and the corpse kept on re-appearing in my inventory list.
>
>	I would drop it on the alter and it would not be in my inventory
>    but after I #offer 'ed it to my god it was back in my inventory.  I 
>    could drop it again and offer it again.  If it makes a difference,
>    I offered it about 30 times and always got  a "Nothing Happens" message.

When you drop corpses on altars, you cannot sacrifice them because you are
no longer in possession of them.  It "reappeared" in your inventory because
you were in AUTO-PICKUP mode, and after a command, you automatically
grabbed any items in the square.  After a real sacrifice (that the god
accepts), the corpse should vanish in a burst of flame.  Gods like fresh
blood over tainted meat, and may not accept certain corpses.  The "Nothing
Happens" message came because you weren't holding the corpse in question.

